  "result": "The quiz is written at `quizzes/0002.json`, and its key is at `keys/0002.json`. It has six questions on O4, \"Workflows, agents and who owns the control flow\".\n\nThere is no lesson on this objective yet, so the quiz is ahead of the lessons.\n\n- **Who owns the control flow:** you read small Python handlers and decide whether each is a workflow or an agent. You also find the one pipeline stage where the model's output decides what runs next.\n- **When a fixed workflow is better:** you pick a design for a nightly job whose steps never change, and compare the cost of an agent loop with a fixed workflow. You also split the assistant's booking and manual-question jobs between a workflow and an agent, given an audit-log need and a model-call cap.\n- **Mix:** three multiple-choice, two short-answer and one numeric question. The scenarios come from the makerspace assistant and backend code.\n\nThe `quiz-reviewer` subagent read the draft twice, and the review ended at the two-pass cap, not with a clean report. I declined one finding. It asked for a different question mix, but q2 is the quiz's one recall-style item and q6 now tests a different thing. The details are in `review-records/0002-quiz.md`.\n\nI couldn't read `keys/`, so I couldn't check which misconception ids quiz 0001 already uses. The new key uses M10 to M17, which are well above any id I could see. If quiz 0001's key defines any of the same ids with other meanings, the grader should reconcile them. Would you like me to confirm that before grading?",
